    {
      "id": "s0101",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Any missing converter? Open an issue or pull request!",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0102",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Deployment",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0103",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Warning",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0104",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you can't login, make sure you are accessing the service over localhost or https otherwise set HTTP_ALLOWED=true",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0105",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "or",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0106",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ensure [[p0]] and [[p1]] match your host user ([[p2]] and [[p3]]) to avoid permission issues on the mapped [[p4]] volume. If you get unable to open database file, verify the directory permissions or run [[p5]] on the path you choose.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "PUID"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "PGID"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "id -u"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "id -g"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "./data"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "text": "chown -R $USER:$USER path"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0107",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Then visit [[p0]] in your browser and create your account. Don't leave it unconfigured and open, as anyone can register the first account.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "http://localhost:3000"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0108",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Environment variables",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0109",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "All are optional, JWT_SECRET is recommended to be set.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0110",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Warning",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0111",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Never expose the service to the internet with ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED or ACCOUNT_REGISTRATION true. Only allow users you trust to access the service.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0112",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Name",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0113",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0114",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Description",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0115",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "JWT_SECRET",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0116",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "when unset it will use the value from randomUUID()",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0117",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A long and secret string used to sign the JSON Web Token",
      "protected": []
    },
